## Fix #824: No validation of signingKey value before storing

### Problem
`setSigningKey` stored any value passed to it without validation. A corrupted export or crafted data injection could persist invalid data, causing silent transaction failures later.

### Fix
Added validation before storing:
```typescript
if (!signingKey) {
  throw new Error('signingKey must not be null or undefined');
}
if (typeof signingKey !== 'object') {
  throw new Error('signingKey must be an object, got: ' + typeof signingKey);
}
```

### Benefit
Immediate, actionable error on invalid signing key data instead of silent data corruption.

