Changing prediction or evaluation group-by fields, or filling missing defaults, could rebuild dashboard rows with new group IDs and implicitly drop selection. This updates the eval dashboard to treat newly affected rows as selected by default while preserving explicit user deselections where possible.

This PR implements #433.

- **Shared selection state sync**
  - Generalize the selection sync logic into a reusable helper for dashboard group selection.
  - Preserve selections for groups that still exist.
  - Auto-select newly introduced groups after regrouping or missing-value default application.

- **Predictions table**
  - Apply the shared selection sync to prediction groups when the Predictions table is rebuilt.
  - Track previously available prediction group IDs so merged/newly created rows stay selected by default.

- **Evaluations table and plots**
  - Keep the same behavior for evaluation groups in the Evaluations table.
  - Reuse the same shared selection-sync logic for evaluation plot group selection.

```html
function syncSelectedGroupIds(selectionState, validGroupIds) {
  if (!(selectionState.availableGroupIds instanceof Set)) {
    selectionState.availableGroupIds = new Set();
  }
  if (selectionState.selectedGroupIds === null) {
    selectionState.selectedGroupIds = new Set(validGroupIds);
  } else {
    const nextSelectedGroupIds = new Set(
      Array.from(selectionState.selectedGroupIds).filter((groupId) => validGroupIds.has(groupId))
    );
    for (const groupId of validGroupIds) {
      if (!selectionState.availableGroupIds.has(groupId)) {
        nextSelectedGroupIds.add(groupId);
      }
    }
    selectionState.selectedGroupIds = nextSelectedGroupIds;
  }
  selectionState.availableGroupIds = new Set(validGroupIds);
}
```

