`CommitDiffActivity` and `ViewFileFragment` each define:


```
mDiffContent.setWebChromeClient(new WebChromeClient() {
    public void onConsoleMessage(...) { ... }

    public boolean shouldOverrideUrlLoading(WebView view, String url) {
        return false;
    }
});
```


`shouldOverrideUrlLoading` is a `WebViewClient` method, not a `WebChromeClient` method, so this override never runs. It is dead code that looks like a routing decision is being made when none actually is.

Both diff / file viewers feed the WebView a fixed `file:///android_asset/` template via `loadDataWithBaseURL` and never navigate, so there is no real `shouldOverrideUrlLoading` to define either.

### Change

Drop the four-line method block in both files. `onConsoleMessage` (the only override that actually applies on `WebChromeClient`) stays where it is.
